1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,031
Production depends on five secondary services.

2
00:00:03,281 --> 00:00:09,450
As maintenance personnel, you will work on all of them, and each has its own safety rules.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,479
One: aspiration.

4
00:00:11,729 --> 00:00:24,450
It controls dust across the plant, protecting worker health, preventing dust explosions and maintaining product quality.

5
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:29,694
Safety first: always follow lock-out tag-out.

6
00:00:29,944 --> 00:00:34,858
Never bypass explosion vents or safety devices.

7
00:00:35,108 --> 00:00:41,450
Dust building up in ductwork is a fire and explosion hazard.

8
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:44,411
Two: compressed air.

9
00:00:44,661 --> 00:00:57,450
It supplies clean, dry air for pneumatic controls, actuators, air-operated equipment and cleaning.

10
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:03,677
Three: electrical installations and the plant control system.

11
00:01:03,927 --> 00:01:11,450
They distribute power, and the control system automates and monitors production.

12
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:16,962
Electrical work is for qualified personnel only.

13
00:01:17,212 --> 00:01:24,563
Follow lock-out tag-out and verify zero energy state before you start.

14
00:01:24,813 --> 00:01:29,450
Arc flash hazards exist at electrical panels.

15
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:33,719
Four: liquid installations.

16
00:01:33,969 --> 00:01:44,450
They store, heat and add liquid ingredients like molasses, fats and oils.

17
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:47,659
Five: steam supply.

18
00:01:47,909 --> 00:01:59,450
It provides steam for conditioning, pelleting, extrusion and heating liquids.

19
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:05,562
Steam systems run at high temperature and pressure.

20
00:02:05,812 --> 00:02:09,778
Burns and scalds are serious hazards.

21
00:02:10,028 --> 00:02:14,450
Never work on a pressurized steam system.

22
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:33,126
Five services: aspiration, compressed air, electrical and control, liquids, and steam.

23
00:02:33,376 --> 00:02:40,604
Know them, and work on them safely.

24
00:02:40,854 --> 00:02:44,450
Now take the quiz.

